# renki-manifest

A manifest read off the disk with its layers. It finds `name.ext` and every
`name.<layer>.ext` beside it or through `meta.overlays.include`, answers the
named predicates from the environment and a shell, stacks the layers by
`renki-config`'s rules, and hands them to a tool's schema with every refusal
naming its file. It reads through the C library into memory the caller gives,
parses with `tomlfuse-parse`, and has a POSIX reader of the same manifests
beside it under `posix/`. On `renki-config` and `tomlfuse-parse`; `renki` and
any tool reading a manifest depend on it. `#![no_std]`, no alloc, unix.
